I built the Brief C phone agent and saved it under slot main-C. The lint shows 0 errors and one live chat turn opens correctly ("Hello, this is the virtual assistant of FB Services. This call is recorded. May I speak with Omar Haddad?"). I didn't test past that first turn or run any cases. I also didn't do the full rule-by-rule recheck against the brief because of the time limit.

The workflow is in `out/main-C.workflow.json`. It has a start node made from the date code, then an opening node that handles third parties and callbacks. Next come an identity node, a silent `get_account` step and a single negotiation node for all accounts, with a close step at the end. The account hook is on `get_account` and `{{date_facts}}` is in every node that deals with dates.

**Where the brief differs from the date facts, I followed the brief.** I changed one setting in the encoded settings string and added code after the account hook. The code itself was not changed.
- **Weekend:** the code's settings treated Saturday and Sunday as the weekend. The brief says Friday and Saturday, so I changed that setting in both the start node and the account hook.
- **Deadline:** the code adds calendar days but never moves the deadline back to the last business day before it, as the brief requires. My added hook code does that.
- **Overdraft floor:** the code took half the arrears without rounding up to a whole unit (387.50 gave 193.75, not 194.00). My added hook code rounds it up. The same code also prepares the two halves of the two-part plan and a one-line summary per account.

**One choice of mine:** the brief says nothing about what to do if the identity or account service fails twice. I made the agent close the call as `no_contact` / `NO_CALLBACK` in that case.

